<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Dynatech cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Dynatech cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Adams, Harkness &amp; Hill analyst Jonathon Stone said he downgraded Dynatech Corp to attractive from buy.</p>
<p>-- said cut his 1998 earnings forecast to $2.55 a share from an early estimate of $2.65 a share.</p>
<p>-- said Dynatech appears to be growing more slowly than expected.</p>
<p>-- On Monday, Dynatech posted a third quarter loss of $0.16 a share, compared with earnings of $0.43 a share last year. The 1996 third quarter results included a $0.74 a share charge for the purchase of incomplete technology at Itronix.</p>
<p>-- Dynatech lost 6-1/2 to 42.</p>
<p>(( -- Wall Street desk 212-859-1730))</p>
